<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 363 0 R
/E (SQL Injection \(SQLi\) occurs when an web application constructs SQL queries using user-supplied input without proper sanitization or parameterization. In the Altoro Mutual demo, we identified that the backend database directly concatenates user input into SQL statements.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
895 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 363 0 R
/E (Specifically, the login endpoint \(or search field\) accepts unvalidated input. When a specific payload is entered, it alters the logic of the underlying SQL query. For example, entering ' OR '1'='1 in the username field can close the original string, add an OR condition that is always true, and bypass authentication checks, allowing the attacker to log in as any user \(often the first admin user found\) without knowing the password.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
